  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-led Approaches to Addressing the Drivers of Violence and  Vulnerability and Promoting Spaces for Conflict Prevention</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The rationale behind the UN Joint Programme is that vulnerability and severe poverty and gender discrimination reinforce fault lines and act as conflict drivers between communities in the Abyei area. Competition over natural resources, especially during migration season, in this context is a main conflict trigger and often increases the risk of reprisal attacks and vicious cycles of violence including targeted attacks on women and children.</narrative>
  </description>
